# DakshAI / NewRelay Development & UI Rules

## Core Principles
1. **Tailwind Only**: Strictly use Tailwind CSS utility classes. Custom CSS, scoped CSS, and inline styles are explicitly forbidden.
2. **Dynamic Theme Colors**: NEVER use hardcoded Tailwind colors (e.g., `bg-blue-100`, `text-[#3B82F6]`). Always map colors to semantic variables (`bg-background`, `bg-card`, `bg-primary`, `text-muted-foreground`, `border-border`) to ensure dark mode compatibility.
3. **AI Naming**: Always use "Relay AI" to refer to the AI system. Translate references to "Captain" to "Relay AI".

## Component Styling Rules
- **Headings**: Section/Page Headings use `text-base font-medium` (16px, 500w). Empty State Headings strictly use `text-[20px] font-[600]`.
- **Ghost Buttons**: Always add a subtle gray border to define boundaries (e.g., `border border-border`). On hover, remove it (`hover:border-transparent`).
- **Modals/Popups**: 
  - Backdrop: `bg-background/80 backdrop-blur-[8px]` (prefer `RELAY_DIALOG_OVERLAY_CLASS` from `relay/modal/constants.js`).
  - Header: `RELAY_MODAL_HEADER_CLASS` — title `text-base font-medium tracking-tight`, description `text-[14px] font-normal text-muted-foreground`, then `border-b border-border/80`. Form fields start below the divider in the body.
  - Content body: `p-6` (or `pt-4 pb-8 px-8` for legacy woot-modal-content migration).
- **Forms (in Modals)**:
  - Field wrapper: `flex flex-col gap-1.5` between label and input/textarea.
  - Labels: `text-[13.5px] font-medium leading-normal text-foreground`.
  - Inputs / textareas: `text-[14px] shadow-sm rounded-md border-border/80 bg-background focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-1 focus-visible:ring-primary/30`.
  - Checkboxes: wrapper `flex items-center gap-3` — strictly no manual top margins (e.g. `mt-0.5`).
  - Prefer `RelayInput`, `RelayTextarea`, and `relay/form/constants.js` tokens.
  - Validation: The primary submit action button MUST remain disabled unless all required fields are correctly filled.
- **Tabs**:
  - Underline tabs (Inbox, list filters, entity details): container `border-b border-border`; inactive `text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground`; active indicator is an absolute **1px** bar `h-px bg-primary` (never `border-b-2` on `<button>`, never `h-0.5`).
  - Pill tabs (`RelayTabs`): muted track, active `bg-background shadow-sm`.
- **Inbox / nested list chrome**:
  - Section labels (Views, Channels): `text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground`.
  - Count badges: `text-[11px] font-semibold`.
  - Website channel icon: `i-lucide-globe`.
  - Tab-row bulk action is **Select All** text, not an icon cluster.
  - Stars: `InboxStarIcon` (same SVG outline/fill). Display chevron `size-3.5`; sliders `size-[18px]`. Row channel well `size-5`, icon `size-3.5`.
- **Dropdowns/Popovers**: 
  - Wrapper: `bg-popover text-popover-foreground shadow-md rounded-md border border-border`.
  - Items: `px-2 py-1.5 text-sm hover:bg-accent hover:text-accent-foreground`.
- **Empty States**: Include a temporary "developer button" at the very bottom to toggle mock data.
- **Native vs Custom**: NEVER rely on unstyled native HTML elements that trigger browser-default popups (like `<select>`, native date pickers). Build or style them to match the UI system.
